":"alef","r":"ā","ipa":"/ɒː/","ex":{"w":"آسمان","v":"آسِمانْ","r":"āsemān","m":"sky","a":"ae8e7ade83f8"}},{"g":"و","name":"vāv","r":"u","ipa":"/uː/","ex":{"w":"دوست","v":"دوسْتْ","r":"dust","m":"friend","a":"4fed18860a95"}},{"g":"ی","name":"ye","r":"i","ipa":"/iː/","ex":{"w":"ماهی","v":"ماهی","r":"māhi","m":"fish","a":"dd4f563e93ae"}}]}],"tips":["Persian is written and read from right to left, but numbers run left to right.","Seven letters never join the letter after them: ا د ذ ر ز ژ و. In دارو (dāru, medicine) all four letters stand apart.","Some sounds have several letters: t = ت ط, s = ث س ص, z = ذ ز ض ظ, h = ح ه, gh = غ ق. Learn the spelling with each word.","Short vowels (a, e, o) are usually not written: کتاب (ketāb, book) is just k-t-ā-b. Learn every word with its pronunciation.","A vowel at the start of a word sits on ا: اسب (asb, horse), ایران (irān). Long ā at the start is written آ: آب (āb, water).","Tanvin ـاً is read -an at the end of some words from Arabic: لطفاً (lotfan, please), حتماً (hatman, definitely)."]}}